TEXT 136 96 Left 2 ;New RMS metering with phasemeatering
TEXT -184 128 Left 2 !.param RN=0.4 LN={1/314.159}
TEXT 648 32 Left 2 ;**********************************************************\n* special transient toolbox stuff:\n**********************************************************\n* dt=Measure of time in ms measured from current zero to voltage zero (for value see left statusline)\n.func dt1(dt) {IF(dt>5m,dt-10m,IF(dt<-5m,dt+10m,dt))}\n.func dt1_60(dt) {IF(dt>4.1667m,dt-8.3333m,IF(dt<-4.1667m,dt+8.3333m,dt))}\n.func t2phi(dt) {dt1(dt)*90/5m}\n.func t2phi60(dt) {dt1_60(dt)*90/4.1667m}\n* apparent power measurement per phase (sfactor=1)\n.func S(ipeak,vpeak) {1.5*ipeak*vpeak/3}\n* aktive power measurement\n.func P50Hz(ipeak,vpeak,ti,tv) {IF((ti-tv)<5m & (ti-tv)>=-5ms,S(ipeak,vpeak)*cos(t2phi(ti-tv)),-S(ipeak,vpeak)*cos(t2phi(ti-tv)))}\n* reactive power measurement ti>tv Qpos ti<tv Qneg\n.func Q50Hz(ipeak,vpeak,ti,tv) {IF((ti-tv)<5m & (ti-tv)>=-5ms,S(ipeak,vpeak)*sin(t2phi((ti-tv))),-S(ipeak,vpeak)*sin(t2phi((ti-tv))))}\n* aktive power measurement\n.func P60Hz(ipeak,vpeak,ti,tv) {IF((ti-tv)<4.1667m & (ti-tv)>=-4.1667m,S(ipeak,vpeak)*cos(t2phi60((ti-tv))),-S(ipeak,vpeak)*cos(t2phi60((ti-tv))))}\n* reactive power measurement ti>tv Qpos ti<tv Qneg\n.func Q60Hz(ipeak,vpeak,ti,tv) {IF((ti-tv)<4.1667m & (ti-tv)>=-4.1667m,S(ipeak,vpeak)*sin(t2phi60((ti-tv))),-S(ipeak,vpeak)*sin(t2phi60((ti-tv))))}\n* IF phii and phiv is measured by phasemeters\n.func dphi(phii,phiv) {phii-phiv}\n.func phy(phii,phiv) {IF(dphi(phii,phiv)<-90,dphi(phii,phiv)+180,dphi(phii,phiv))}\n.func phi(phii,phiv){IF(dphi(phii,phiv)>90,dphi(phii,phiv)-180,phy(phii,phiv))}\n.func P1(phii,phiv,ipeak,vpeak) {IF(dphi(phii,phiv)<90 & dphi(phii,phiv)>-90,S(ipeak,vpeak)*cos(V(phi)*pi/180),-S(ipeak,vpeak)*cos(V(phi)*pi/180))}\n.func Q1(phii,phiv,ipeak,vpeak) {IF(dphi(phii,phiv)<90 & dphi(phii,phiv)>-90,-S(ipeak,vpeak)*sin(V(phi)*pi/180),S(ipeak,vpeak)*sin(V(phi)*pi/180))}
TEXT 648 -160 Left 4 ;Copy/Paste this in the plot.defs file if \nnot yet present there\nthan restart ltspice to make the changes active\nFrom now on you can enter at the waveformviewer as trace:\nP50Hz(Ipeak,Vpeak,timeI,timeV) and\nQ50Hz(Ipeak,Vpeak,timeI,timeV) \nP50Hz(775,93.26k,440m,441.28m)\nQ50Hz(775,93.26k,440m,441.28m)\nHINT: In the .meas file the 3phase power is measured\nIn the P50Hz,Q50Hz traces the 1phase power is measured
TEXT -584 80 Left 2 ;1) Measurement of ipeak and vpeak in the waveformviewer\n \n2) Measurement of ti=time of current max and tv=time of voltage max\n    in the waveformviewer on the point in the network you want to measure P,Q\n    U and I should be at the same y-axis therefore I must be\n    multiplied by 1V/1A*fact.\n  \n3) Add trace P50Hz(ipeak,vpeak,ti,tv) in the waveformviewer \n    for active power at 50Hz ore P60Hz(..) for 60Hz \n   The reacitve power is Q50Hz(..) and Q60Hz(..)
TEXT -576 0 Left 4 ;Measurement of P,Q with the\nwaveformviewer and with\nplot.defs (Plott settings/Edit\nplot.defs File)
TEXT -576 -160 Left 2 !.meas TRAN Upeak MAX V(n012) FROM {start} TO {stop}\n.meas TRAN Ipeak MAX  Ix(U21:in) FROM {start} TO {stop}\n \n.meas TRAN T1 FIND time WHEN V(n012)=0 TD={start}\n.meas TRAN T2 FIND time WHEN Ix(U21:in)=0 TD={start}\n.meas TRAN dt PARAM t2-t1\n.meas TRAN dt1 PARAM If(dt>5m,dt-10m,IF(dt<-5m,dt+10m,dt))\n.meas TRAN t2phi PARAM dt1*90/5m\n.meas TRAN S PARAM 1.5*Upeak*Ipeak\n.meas TRAN P50Hz PARAM IF(dt<5m & dt>=-5ms,S*cos(t2phi),-S*cos(t2phi))\n.meas TRAN Q50Hz PARAM IF(dt<5m & dt>=-5ms,S*sin(t2phi),-S*sin(t2phi))
TEXT -576 -176 Left 2 !.param start=435m stop={start+20m}
TEXT -576 -232 Left 2 ;The same with .meas script (for the result see spice error.log)\nYou can also execute a external meas script with\nFile / Execute Meas Script / PQ_meatering.meas \nYou have to select the waveformviewer window before !!
TEXT -312 -184 Left 2 ;To meas all cases of +P,+Q,-P,-Q it is necessary \nto adapt the start time again to met the proper I,V=0 condition
TEXT 376 192 Left 2 ;Three phase power is \nmeasured
LINE Normal 560 112 -192 -176 2
LINE Normal 560 112 560 112 2
